# Copy to `_ops/.scrub-terms.local` and put your own terms in it.
# That file is gitignored: it never gets published, which is the whole point.
#
# One term per line, case-insensitive, matched as a literal substring.
# Blank lines and comment lines are ignored. A line that is only a hex value,
# such as the third example below, is treated as a term rather than a comment.
#
# Put here anything your copy must never leak: a client name, an internal
# codename, a brand hex value, a mailing list, a partner you are under NDA with.
#
# Do NOT commit the filled-in version. A list of terms you are trying to hide is
# itself a disclosure: it names each one AND asserts that each one is sensitive.
clientcorp
internal-codename
D4F0C2
announce-all@
